---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout
  title="Compound Interest Calculator India | Simple vs Compound | Arthavi"
  description="Free compound interest calculator. Compare simple vs compound interest with monthly, quarterly, half-yearly and annual compounding. See the power of compounding visually."
  keywords="compound interest calculator, simple vs compound interest calculator, monthly compounding calculator, compound interest formula India, interest calculator"
  breadcrumb={{ items: [{ name: "Home", url: "https://arthavi.com/" }, { name: "Calculators", url: "https://arthavi.com/calculators" }, { name: "Compound Interest Calculator", url: "https://arthavi.com/compound-interest-calculator" }] }}
  schema={JSON.stringify({
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@graph": [
      { "@type": "WebPage", "@id": "https://arthavi.com/compound-interest-calculator", "name": "Compound Interest Calculator India | Simple vs Compound", "inLanguage": "en-IN", "dateModified": "2025-07-24" },
      { "@type": "WebApplication", "name": "Compound Interest Calculator", "url": "https://arthavi.com/compound-interest-calculator", "applicationCategory": "FinanceApplication", "offers": { "@type": "Offer", "price": "0", "priceCurrency": "INR" } },
      { "@type": "FAQPage", "mainEntity": [
        { "@type": "Question", "name": "What is the compound interest formula?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Compound Interest formula: A = P × (1 + r/n)^(n×t), where A = Maturity amount, P = Principal, r = Annual interest rate (decimal), n = Compounding frequency per year (12 for monthly, 4 for quarterly), t = Time in years. Compound Interest = A − P." } },
        { "@type": "Question", "name": "What is the difference between simple and compound interest?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Simple Interest = P × r × t / 100 (interest only on principal). Compound Interest calculates interest on principal + accumulated interest each period. Example: ₹1 lakh at 10% for 10 years = ₹1 lakh SI, but ₹1.59 lakh CI (annual) or ₹1.70 lakh CI (monthly). Compound interest is far superior for long-term wealth building." } }
      ]}
    ]
  })}
>
  <main style="padding-top:5.5rem;">
    <section class="calc-page-hero">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="calc-breadcrumb"><a href="/calculators/">Calculators</a><span>→</span><span>Compound Interest Calculator</span></div>
        <div class="calc-hero-content">
          <div class="calc-hero-left">
            <span class="calc-badge" style="background:rgba(236,72,153,.12);border:1px solid rgba(236,72,153,.25);color:#f472b6;">📊 Interest Calculator</span>
            <h1>Compound Interest Calculator</h1>
            <p class="calc-hero-desc"><strong>Compound interest</strong> is interest calculated on both the initial principal and the accumulated interest from previous periods. Formula: <code>A = P × (1 + r/n)^(n×t)</code>. Albert Einstein reportedly called it "the eighth wonder of the world."</p>
            <div class="ci-formula-boxes">
              <div class="ci-formula-box">
                <div class="cf-title" style="color:#f472b6">Compound Interest</div>
                <div class="cf-formula">A = P × (1 + r/n)^(n×t)</div>
                <div class="cf-eg">₹1L @ 10% × 10yr = ₹1,70,070</div>
              </div>
              <div class="ci-formula-box">
                <div class="cf-title" style="color:var(--text-muted)">Simple Interest</div>
                <div class="cf-formula">SI = P × r × t / 100</div>
                <div class="cf-eg">₹1L @ 10% × 10yr = ₹1,00,000</div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="calc-hero-right">
            <div class="calc-panel glass-panel">
              <h2 class="calc-panel-title">Compound Interest Calculator</h2>
              <div class="calc-inputs">
                <div class="calc-input-group">
                  <label>Principal Amount</label>
                  <div class="input-row"><span class="input-prefix">₹</span><input type="number" id="ci-principal" value="100000" min="1000" oninput="calcCI()"></div>
                  <input type="range" id="ci-p-slider" min="10000" max="10000000" step="10000" value="100000" class="calc-slider">
                </div>
                <div class="calc-input-group">
                  <label>Annual Interest Rate</label>
                  <div class="input-row"><input type="number" id="ci-rate" value="10" min="0.1" max="50" step="0.25" oninput="calcCI()"><span class="input-suffix">%</span></div>
                  <input type="range" id="ci-r-slider" min="1" max="30" step="0.25" value="10" class="calc-slider">
                </div>
                <div class="calc-input-group">
                  <label>Time Period</label>
                  <div class="input-row"><input type="number" id="ci-time" value="10" min="1" max="50" oninput="calcCI()"><span class="input-suffix">Years</span></div>
                  <input type="range" id="ci-t-slider" min="1" max="40" step="1" value="10" class="calc-slider">
                </div>
                <div class="calc-input-group">
                  <label>Compounding Frequency</label>
                  <select id="ci-freq" onchange="calcCI()" style="width:100%;background:rgba(255,255,255,.04);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.1);border-radius:10px;padding:.65rem .75rem;color:var(--text-head);font-size:.9rem;font-family:inherit;outline:none;">
                    <option value="12">Monthly</option>
                    <option value="4" selected>Quarterly</option>
                    <option value="2">Half-Yearly</option>
                    <option value="1">Annually</option>
                  </select>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="ci-results">
                <div class="ci-compare-row">
                  <div class="ci-compare-box" style="border-color:rgba(236,72,153,.3)">
                    <div class="result-label" style="color:#f472b6">Compound Interest</div>
                    <div class="result-value" style="color:#f472b6" id="ci-ci">₹1,70,070</div>
                    <div class="ci-maturity-sub" id="ci-maturity">Total: ₹2,70,070</div>
                  </div>
                  <div class="ci-compare-box">
                    <div class="result-label">Simple Interest</div>
                    <div class="result-value" id="ci-si">₹1,00,000</div>
                    <div class="ci-maturity-sub" id="si-total">Total: ₹2,00,000</div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div class="ci-gain-note" id="ci-gain">🎯 Compound interest earns ₹70,070 more than simple interest!</div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="faq-section">
      <div class="container">
        <h2 class="faq-heading">Compound Interest FAQs</h2>
        <div class="faq-list">
          <div class="faq-item" onclick="this.classList.toggle('open')"><div class="faq-q">What is the compound interest formula? <span class="faq-icon">+</span></div><div class="faq-a">A = P × (1 + r/n)^(n×t), where A = final amount, P = principal, r = annual rate (decimal), n = compounding times/year, t = years. CI = A − P.</div></div>
          <div class="faq-item" onclick="this.classList.toggle('open')"><div class="faq-q">How much does ₹1 lakh become in 10 years at 12%? <span class="faq-icon">+</span></div><div class="faq-a">₹1 lakh at 12% for 10 years: Annually = ₹3,10,585 | Quarterly = ₹3,26,204 | Monthly = ₹3,30,039. This is the power of compounding frequency — monthly compounding gives ₹19,454 more than annual.</div></div>
          <div class="faq-item" onclick="this.classList.toggle('open')"><div class="faq-q">What is the Rule of 72? <span class="faq-icon">+</span></div><div class="faq-a">The Rule of 72 estimates how long it takes for money to double: Years to double = 72 ÷ Interest Rate. At 8% = 9 years, at 12% = 6 years, at 15% = 4.8 years. It's a quick mental math shortcut for compound interest approximation.</div></div>
          <div class="faq-item" onclick="this.classList.toggle('open')"><div class="faq-q">Which investments offer compound interest in India? <span class="faq-icon">+</span></div><div class="faq-a">Investments with compounding: (1) FD — quarterly compounding, (2) PPF — annual compounding at 7.1%, (3) Mutual Funds/ELSS — market-linked, effectively compounds annually, (4) NPS — market-linked compounding, (5) Recurring Deposits (RD) — quarterly compounding. Savings bank accounts offer simple interest quarterly.</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="related-section">
      <div class="container">
        <h2 class="related-heading">Related Calculators</h2>
        <div class="related-grid">
          <a href="/fd-calculator/" class="related-card"><span class="related-icon">🏦</span><div><strong>FD Calculator</strong><p>Fixed Deposit with compounding</p></div></a>
          <a href="/sip-calculator/" class="related-card"><span class="related-icon">📈</span><div><strong>SIP Calculator</strong><p>Monthly investment compounding</p></div></a>
          <a href="/ppf-calculator/" class="related-card"><span class="related-icon">🏛️</span><div><strong>PPF Calculator</strong><p>Annual compounding at 7.1%</p></div></a>
          <a href="/emi-calculator/" class="related-card"><span class="related-icon">💳</span><div><strong>EMI Calculator</strong><p>Reducing balance interest</p></div></a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>

<script is:inline>
function fmt(n){return '₹'+Math.round(n).toLocaleString('en-IN');}
['ci-p-slider','ci-r-slider','ci-t-slider'].forEach((sid,i)=>{const ids=['ci-principal','ci-rate','ci-time'];const s=document.getElementById(sid);const inp=document.getElementById(ids[i]);if(s&&inp){inp.addEventListener('input',()=>{s.value=inp.value;calcCI();});s.addEventListener('input',()=>{inp.value=s.value;calcCI();});}});
function calcCI(){
  const P=parseFloat(document.getElementById('ci-principal').value)||0;
  const r=parseFloat(document.getElementById('ci-rate').value)||0;
  const t=parseFloat(document.getElementById('ci-time').value)||0;
  const n=parseFloat(document.getElementById('ci-freq').value)||4;
  const A=P*Math.pow(1+r/100/n,n*t);
  const CI=A-P;
  const SI=P*r*t/100;
  document.getElementById('ci-ci').textContent=fmt(CI);
  document.getElementById('ci-maturity').textContent='Total: '+fmt(A);
  document.getElementById('ci-si').textContent=fmt(SI);
  document.getElementById('si-total').textContent='Total: '+fmt(P+SI);
  const gain=CI-SI;
  document.getElementById('ci-gain').textContent=gain>0?`🎯 Compound interest earns ${fmt(gain)} more than simple interest!`:'';
}
window.calcCI=calcCI;
document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded',calcCI);
</script>

<style>
  .calc-page-hero{padding:2rem 0 3rem;}.calc-breadcrumb{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.5rem;font-size:.82rem;color:var(--text-muted);margin-bottom:2rem;}.calc-breadcrumb a{color:var(--text-muted);text-decoration:none;}.calc-badge{display:inline-block;font-size:.78rem;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;padding:.25rem .8rem;border-radius:100px;margin-bottom:1rem;}.calc-hero-content{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1.1fr;gap:3rem;align-items:start;}.calc-hero-left h1{font-size:clamp(1.8rem,4vw,2.6rem);font-weight:800;color:var(--text-head);margin-bottom:1rem;}.calc-hero-desc{color:var(--text-muted);line-height:1.75;font-size:.93rem;margin-bottom:1.25rem;}.calc-hero-desc strong{color:var(--text-head);}.calc-hero-desc code{background:rgba(236,72,153,.1);border:1px solid rgba(236,72,153,.2);color:#f472b6;padding:.15rem .5rem;border-radius:6px;font-size:.82rem;display:block;margin-top:.5rem;}.ci-formula-boxes{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:.75rem;}.ci-formula-box{background:rgba(255,255,255,.025);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.07);border-radius:12px;padding:1rem;}.cf-title{font-size:.72rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em;margin-bottom:.4rem;}.cf-formula{font-size:.82rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--text-head);font-family:monospace;margin-bottom:.3rem;}.cf-eg{font-size:.75rem;color:var(--text-muted);}.calc-panel{padding:1.75rem;border-radius:20px;}.calc-panel-title{font-size:1.05rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--text-head);margin-bottom:1.25rem;}.calc-inputs{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:.9rem;margin-bottom:1.25rem;}.calc-input-group label{display:block;font-size:.78rem;color:var(--text-muted);margin-bottom:.35rem;font-weight:500;}.input-row{display:flex;align-items:center;background:rgba(255,255,255,.04);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.1);border-radius:10px;overflow:hidden;transition:border-color .2s;}.input-row:focus-within{border-color:rgba(236,72,153,.4);}.input-prefix{padding:.6rem .75rem;font-size:.85rem;color:var(--text-muted);background:rgba(255,255,255,.02);border-right:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.06);flex-shrink:0;}.input-suffix{padding:.6rem .75rem;font-size:.82rem;color:var(--text-muted);border-left:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.06);flex-shrink:0;}.input-row input{flex:1;background:none;border:none;outline:none;padding:.6rem .75rem;color:var(--text-head);font-size:.9rem;font-family:inherit;width:100%;}.calc-slider{width:100%;margin-top:.4rem;accent-color:#ec4899;}.ci-results{background:rgba(236,72,153,.05);border:1px solid rgba(236,72,153,.15);border-radius:14px;padding:1.25rem;}.ci-compare-row{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:.75rem;margin-bottom:.75rem;}.ci-compare-box{background:rgba(255,255,255,.025);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.07);border-radius:10px;padding:1rem;text-align:center;}.result-label{font-size:.72rem;color:var(--text-muted);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em;margin-bottom:.25rem;}.result-value{font-size:1.2rem;font-weight:800;color:var(--text-head);font-family:'Outfit',sans-serif;margin-bottom:.2rem;}.ci-maturity-sub{font-size:.72rem;color:var(--text-muted);}.ci-gain-note{text-align:center;font-size:.85rem;font-weight:600;color:#f472b6;}.faq-section{padding:3rem 0;border-top:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.05);}.faq-heading{font-size:1.4rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--text-head);margin-bottom:1.5rem;}.faq-list{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:.75rem;max-width:800px;}.faq-item{background:rgba(255,255,255,.025);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.07);border-radius:12px;overflow:hidden;cursor:pointer;transition:border-color .2s;}.faq-item.open{border-color:rgba(236,72,153,.3);}.faq-q{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;padding:1rem 1.25rem;font-size:.9rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--text-head);gap:1rem;}.faq-icon{font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--text-muted);transition:transform .2s;flex-shrink:0;}.faq-item.open .faq-icon{transform:rotate(45deg);}.faq-a{max-height:0;overflow:hidden;transition:max-height .3s ease;padding:0 1.25rem;font-size:.86rem;color:var(--text-muted);line-height:1.75;}.faq-item.open .faq-a{max-height:300px;padding-bottom:1.25rem;}.related-section{padding:3rem 0 5rem;border-top:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.05);}.related-heading{font-size:1.2rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--text-head);margin-bottom:1.25rem;}.related-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(200px,1fr));gap:1rem;}.related-card{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:1rem;background:rgba(255,255,255,.025);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.07);border-radius:12px;padding:1rem 1.25rem;text-decoration:none;transition:all .2s;}.related-card:hover{border-color:rgba(236,72,153,.3);transform:translateY(-2px);}.related-icon{font-size:1.5rem;flex-shrink:0;}.related-card strong{display:block;font-size:.86rem;color:var(--text-head);margin-bottom:.15rem;}.related-card p{font-size:.73rem;color:var(--text-muted);margin:0;}@media(max-width:900px){.calc-hero-content{grid-template-columns:1fr;}.ci-formula-boxes{grid-template-columns:1fr;}.ci-compare-row{grid-template-columns:1fr;}}
</style>
